{% macro causal_issue_field_rules(include_memory_fields=false) %}


`issue_type`: opening_causal_gap / missing_causal_transition / event_without_cause / unmotivated_decision / question_resolved_too_early / question_ignored{% if include_memory_fields %} / causal_contradiction{% endif %}

`issue_id`: Can be left empty on first discovery, generated by system; when verifying prior_issue unresolved, must retain prior_issue's issue_id.

`severity`: critical / high / medium / low

`location` **Must start with paragraph number**, format `Paragraph N` or `Paragraph N-M` (counting from first non-empty paragraph in body text, 1-based), can add parenthetical clarification after paragraph number.
Example: `Paragraph 5`, `Paragraph 12-14`, `Paragraph 1 (opening continuity)`, `Paragraph 23 (black-clothed figure reveals identity)`.
⚠️ Purely descriptive positioning prohibited (e.g., "turning point" / "middle section"), otherwise downstream fixes cannot be precisely located.

`paragraph_start` / `paragraph_end` must match `location` paragraph numbers; `location_confidence` uses 0-1 to indicate positioning certainty; `anchor_type` uses explicit_para / evidence_exact / evidence_fuzzy / location_parsed / inferred_scope.

`fix_mode`: replace / insert / window / fulltext. Missing causal continuity uses insert; event foreshadowing/decision motivation/turn issues use window; only structural contradictions that cannot be positioned use fulltext.

`evidence` must include at least 20 continuous characters of original body text for downstream problem paragraph positioning.

`evidence_quote` fill in without `[paragraph N]` marker's exact text substring; if the issue is missing content with no quotable original text, may leave empty but must provide paragraph number and insert/window repair mode.
{% endmacro %}